{"title":"Mock AIME 4 2005-2006/Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.mathlinks.ro/Forum/latexrender/pictures/2ea0ce047615395691113a82d6c190b3.gif\">http://www.mathlinks.ro/Forum/latexrender/pictures/2ea0ce047615395691113a82d6c190b3.gif</a>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>1. A 5-digit number is leet if and only if the sum of the first 2 digits, the sum of the last 2 digits and the middle digit are equal. How many 5-digit leet numbers exist?\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>2. Qin Shi Huang wants to count the number of warriors he has to invade China. He puts his warriors into lines with the most people such that they have even length. The people left over are the remainder. He makes 2 lines, with a remainder of 1, 3 lines with a remainder of 2, 4 lines with a remainder of 3, 5 lines with a remainder of 4, and 6 lines with a remainder of 5. Find the minimum number of warriors that he has. \n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>3. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c073f8a05257a19c2dacc368858763bb44fa3747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is a regular tetrahedron. Tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40db9b6f10ff583906d78a06a76e08e04381bc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is formed by connecting the centers of the faces of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c073f8a05257a19c2dacc368858763bb44fa3747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />. Generally, a new tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1ef39be9a742204eb7347c5d32c9941e98c69d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> is formed by connecting the centers of the faces of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f4341a1efbe1a890de160de023b4e4b84ef444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/744280a1131dbc09035f25e742e47d526d6e64fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is the volume of tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f4341a1efbe1a890de160de023b4e4b84ef444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/a/4dae1f507ee3d394e5658b19b634ae128d78b66f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{V_{2006}}{V_1}=\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"84\" height=\"40\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are coprime positive integers, find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>4. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/ceffaf884beaf2bb342a67713b15b60a85e36413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)=\\sum_{i=1}^{20}(-x)^{20-i}(x+i)^i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"214\" height=\"50\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be the product of the roots. How many digits are does <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b45a7758ce77d8f85fa41c9ac8e5a899928a97d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor K \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"19\" /> have where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06681f5b345750104366c512078960fee8d81b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> denotes the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>5. A parabola <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aa9a1c4ce4ce5020ddafb198a6f99ba2a22d154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P: y=x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> is rotated <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8efc4595ab8d0d7d43d5ec1988b1b7dc8ecc7fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$135$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> degrees clockwise about the origin to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3545551b3d62c4e23d5df7352a55602d0aa9adcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. This image is translated upward <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/a/a9a0b193ef5187e1a46edbccb70cc5e310fdf15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8+\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"43\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c8b3ed35fad6a211ca033d7daa4ab7fe61a8ea3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;&#39;$\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/1/b819f4e0d53e3c365149191c2698204cd2418fee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A: (0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/c/f0cbb9521de49314ffa1216fcafb3955c48bf4d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B: (256,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is in Quadrant I, on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c8b3ed35fad6a211ca033d7daa4ab7fe61a8ea3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;&#39;$\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. If the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is at a maximum, it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a0d8fcd576becce85b26ba77c26f2edf904e529.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\sqrt{b}+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"19\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is square free, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>6. Define a sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dcaefb2e004908026d4d5bb8397a488831fd7a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=2006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/6/0e69a466b724877128f77b1b7e24eb6900caf1c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1}=(n+1)^{a_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/1/b0181bd28a5070ce1858fc7618ce017b130c234f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2007}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>7. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is a function that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fec208480cb71a45f97e476439c06c387133840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3f(x)=2x+1-f(\\frac{1}{1-x})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"211\" height=\"37\" /> for all defined <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Suppose that the sum of the zeros of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/220addcdf5a87cfd99ce7fb339322351df461205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are coprime positive integers, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/376d94f98082f674c2a94a704c6cb1efb746dc71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2+n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>8. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a solution to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab80b0570e600761cf6ac2326c7b2e20798a9e7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+\\frac{1}{x}=\\frac{ \\sin210^{\\circ} }{\\sin285^{\\circ} }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"137\" height=\"39\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c48b6b3d5dfa51754122733be0493af4eea039.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{R^{2006}}+R^{2006}=A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"146\" height=\"37\" /> find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec1b38f7da5b3d93abb4e1bf4a4c031c3f6645e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor A^{10} \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06681f5b345750104366c512078960fee8d81b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> is the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>9. Zeus, Athena, and Posideon arrive at Mount Olympus at a random time between 12:00 pm and 12:00 am, and stay for 3 hours. All three hours does not need to fall within 12 pm to 12 am. If any of the 2 gods see each other during 12 pm to 12 am, it will be a good day. The probability of it being a good day is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are coprime positive integers, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>10. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689beb8aca8e3f4550a4d0d8153e88c0133c6f5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S= \\tan^2{1^{\\circ}}+\\tan^2{3^{\\circ}}+\\tan^2{5^{\\circ}}+...+\\tan^2{87^{\\circ}}+\\tan^2{89^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"446\" height=\"16\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. \n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>11. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a9b1d0308432fae3b6fc4a410db4580549b2996.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C= 90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />. A point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies inside the triangle such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a8a6f64c24aa410e1ffc0486291c74746af4097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP=33$\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/7/f177100e7fcd4a369a7bba1d424ac239f512a6cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CP=28\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f135b6a5c94953923cf10224908119f2c80ef687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP=65$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b9116007a90d8b496b3a9aa7920304e0d94a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2A$\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>12. There exists a line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> with points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, not on the line is such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc7fd747e34d640784f12700c345d69197d22b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AF}=6$\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/7/07792c575f3b32a0458c11d4834d2b346ff67cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}=\\frac{36}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/4294bd44af48c23d24086be5d89144fd3aefdd3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE}=\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"79\" height=\"41\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/e/69e6c23a146a60b5b021c49639fb13ab0566f578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AEF &gt; 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" />. Construct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411ef29ce6c32ab71534dfd3319a6fe72af9c5ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> on ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cab46d4c87780bff7c86776c76d858312a86f941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\overline{AE})(\\overline{AE&#39;})=36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/6/946f2df8d0afea46106834eed826cafd9f2f9470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{FE&#39;}=3$\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a11069cdf81eb849dbeaf184b1f87d32bf89d9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AG}=7$\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/0/1c0b6d3812ab02d096ba2adf4509a830d7aacf6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2*(\\overline{E&#39;G})=a+\\sqrt{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"22\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are integers, then find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>13. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/939af119d32862fdc3faa04eefe05765f0621c26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle VA_0A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" /> is isosceles with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad0f1f008df3628d8ea8c06250a2c3ffeabc3008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{{A_1A_0}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" />. Construct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a8ae66ded7f33f9385a37c9cadfb82720013d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/c/f9cd8b552692ceea70c0c4e4475b425742ce26d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{{A_0V}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/54555c6cb13d520a5df83b864b956115b3618955.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{A_0A_1}=\\overline{A_1A_2}=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. Construct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791fe65c9d1ed7d8ed33a5025f40c5c7f9e476af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/f/6df167ab114361e07621f288e92809a7f89eedcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{A_1V}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf54a406c50e0dcc110a8b7201779bd4354a100.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\overline{A_2A_3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />. Contiue this pattern: construct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/f/b0f5c50b1b33dd90a0f99f0013d13ee886bb98f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{A_{2n}A_{2n+1}}=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"19\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/3148797b158d3b303c10ed3b2bd0aa029608fc94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{2n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" /> on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe1721c18a4266ba22d3d82d227d19543664c175.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{VA_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df6d7ecae1512b7ed35713cac354f67c3ed751aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{A_{2n+1}A_{2n+2}}=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"19\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e055e80a32f5a51f4b0c95a10a8a188fca7506e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{2n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08b98d94732f70e14efd55b8657a8fc0246a4d93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{VA_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />. The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1eccfbd65334353f671fb71c27b9b9f2c689b0bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> do not coincide and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/754a57e24dc610b6fa5dfa967624b3c07e1193aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle VA_1A_0=90-\\frac{1}{2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"173\" height=\"37\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/7553256f94a2ce1069471dfe7c43bf8b7215ab90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> is the last point you can construct on the perimeter of the triangle. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. \n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>14. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the probability that if you flip a fair coin, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> heads will occur before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> tails. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/6/6b60549d565b69a94a782d2cb34e2b4d4f60067d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"56\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>15. A regular 61-gon with verticies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a8ae66ded7f33f9385a37c9cadfb82720013d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791fe65c9d1ed7d8ed33a5025f40c5c7f9e476af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />,...<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b5aea7be5b77902f6dea7978478123d05b27bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> is inscribed in a circle with a radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e0651cc73d2c6259a8596bafa7c88882ae1320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\overline{A_1A_2})(\\overline{A_1A_3})(\\overline{A_1A_4})...(\\overline{A_1A_{61}})=r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"279\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/400ee6242229a94abc6bd8838b4db25021ee6cf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^{2006}=\\frac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"71\" height=\"36\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are coprime positive integers, find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/170200756543596efeb46fca1cf29a617e8c9192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_2005-2006/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 2005-2006/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006/Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2005-2006\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2005-2006\">Mock AIME 4 2005-2006</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME\" title=\"Mock AIME\">Mock AIME</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=70988\">Here is the page on AoPS</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018100311\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.069 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.092 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 708/1000000\nPost‐expand include